<title>LUXEMBOURG: Sweden FinMin sees no extra pressure to join ERM.</title>
<headline>Sweden FinMin sees no extra pressure to join ERM.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's Finance Minister Erik Asbrink said on Monday pressure on Sweden to join Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) has not increased in the wake of Finland's decision to join over the weekend.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no increased pressure on Sweden,&quot; Asbrink told Reuters outside the EU finance ministers' meeting in Luxembourg.  </p>
<p>The Swedish government has frequently said ERM adhesion is not on the agenda.</p>
<p>-- Fredrik Dahl, Luxembourg newsroom +32-2-287 6811</p>
